  "notes": [
    "The producer uses the existing A14 deterministic package writer and SDK PackageClosure/buildTransitive task, including exact [V] NativeWeave dependency edges. No new resolver or shared packaging change was introduced.",
    "Both .proto service clients and DTO pairs are generated by Grpc.Tools2.85.0/Google.Protobuf3.36.2. Application-defined IGeneratedGrpcService adapters directly bind closed generic NativeWeave methods. The grpc-dotnet2.85.0 dependency is only the independent demo client.",
    "The ordinary NuGet consumer contains no ProjectReference and locally terminates parent Directory.Build imports. Its own NuGet cache and explicit source mapping/audit remain enabled. Real Rust tool directories were removed from PATH and failing traps detect attempted Rust invocation; no trap fired. The maintainer machine does have Rust, so this is not a pristine-machine claim.",
    "Baseline JIT and NativeAOT run minimal, advanced HTTP2-clear and advanced rustls TLS modes. A real new protobuf tag field and handler/client change are then regenerated, built and executed in JIT and NativeAOT with unchanged packages/native asset. Both changed executable hashes differ from baseline.",
    "Binary input hashes are captured before each execution and checked unchanged immediately after. The baseline JIT directory is later rebuilt for the ordinary edit; its pre-execution executable hash and immutable source/lock/config snapshot remain in snapshots/jit. Baseline AOT/published, edited JIT/AOT, packages and native bytes remain locally available. Reproduce baseline JIT by restoring snapshots/jit source/config into the same consumer location and executing the recorded locked-restore/build commands against the unchanged local feed.",
    "MaxDecodedMessageBytes is decompressed complete-message bytes. GrpcMarshaller is explicit application SPI; decoder DTO graph/private allocations remain application-owned. The guide documents separately pregranted framework/native copies and writer overlap without a zero-allocation claim.",
    "Parent owns B18 full native/managed semantic acceptance, API/XML checks, Plan integration, PRs and merge. This child receipt covers its assigned documentation/sample/package subset only; no other platform or final pristine release gate is claimed."
  ],
